userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: The line integral of a scalar function along a curve is defined as the limit of Riemann sums Σ f(P*_k) Δs_k as the partition is refined, and this limit is independent of where the sample point P*_k is chosen within each subarc.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): A line integral is the limit of density-times-arc-length Riemann sums as the partition is refined, and that limit is the same no matter which point of each subarc you sample.
DEMO STEPS: 3 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

FULL BLUEPRINT:
{
  "concept": "The line integral of a scalar function along a curve is defined as the limit of Riemann sums Σ f(P*_k) Δs_k as the partition is refined, and this limit is independent of where the sample point P*_k is chosen within each subarc.",
  "figureType": "diagram",
  "elements": [
    "left curve from P = P0 (bottom-left) to Q = Pn (top-right), drawn as a smooth blue arc with a loop, in 2D projection of a 3D space curve",
    "partition points P1, P2, P3, ..., P_{n-1} as blue dots along the left curve, count controlled by slider n",
    "endpoint labels 'P = P0' and 'Q = Pn'",
    "highlighted kth subarc between P_{k-1} and P_k on the left curve",
    "label 'Δs_k' with double-headed arrow spanning the kth subarc",
    "label 'Mass ΔM_k' with arrow pointing to the kth subarc",
    "large curved zoom arrow (cream/tan) from the kth subarc to the right inset",
    "right inset: isolated blue subarc from P_{k-1} to P_k with 'Δs_k' double-headed arrow above it",
    "red draggable sample point P*_k on the inset subarc, labeled 'P*_k(x*_k, y*_k, z*_k)'",
    "formula box at bottom: 'ΔM_k ≈ f(x*_k, y*_k, z*_k) Δs_k'",
    "live Riemann-sum readout 'Σ f(P*_k) Δs_k = <value>' and the exact line-integral value '∫_C f ds = <value>' for comparison"
